<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">19 July in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 19 July, from 711 to 1979.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">711</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tariq ibn Ziyad defeats King Roderic at Guadalete</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Umayyad forces under Tariq ibn Ziyad defeated and killed the Visigothic king Roderic, by the traditional date. Within a few years most of Iberia was under Muslim rule, the beginning of al-Andalus.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tariq-ibn-ziyad">Tariq ibn Ziyad</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1553</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mary Tudor is proclaimed Queen of England in London</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">As support for Lady Jane Grey collapsed, the Privy Council proclaimed Mary queen to cheering crowds. England's first undisputed queen regnant restored Catholicism and burned some 280 Protestants.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catholicism">Catholicism</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1848</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Seneca Falls Convention opens</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Elizabeth Cady Stanton and Lucretia Mott opened the first women's rights convention in the United States. Its Declaration of Sentiments, stating that 'all men and women are created equal', launched the suffrage movement.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1870</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">France declares war on Prussia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Provoked by Bismarck's edited Ems Dispatch, Napoleon III's government declared war on Prussia. Within months France was defeated, the Second Empire fell and the German Empire was proclaimed at Versailles.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon-iii">Napoleon III</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1979</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Sandinista rebels take power in Nicaragua</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Two days after Anastasio Somoza Debayle fled, Sandinista forces entered Managua, ending the Somoza family's 43-year rule. The revolution soon drew the US into backing the Contra insurgency.</p></li></ol>
